#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""uniclaude-brain-daily — the uniclaude lane's producer pass.

Durable, reusable grants-ops METHOD only. This box runs Uniswap Foundation client
work, so this lane is narrower than the others: the transferable rule may travel,
the client material under it may not.

Rules this script enforces, per the lane contract:
  - an explicit source allow-list, never a directory sweep, and each source declares
    the STRUCTURE it may lift (rule blocks, named sections, a fenced framework, prose)
  - four line filters drop any surviving line carrying a money figure, a client
    record id, a contact detail, or an applicant/grantee organisation name
  - the finished body is re-scanned for secrets, money and contacts; a body that
    still trips is DROPPED WHOLE and logged loudly — never redacted and shipped
  - idempotent: a source whose DISTILLED body is unchanged produces no capture
  - bounded: bodies cap at 12KB with a pointer to the full source on this host
  - `~/.claude/secrets/` is never read and never captured

The applicant deny-list is derived, not memorised: the calibration corpus declares
its exemplars in `### N. <Name> — VERDICT` headings, so the script harvests those
names at runtime and drops any output line carrying one. New exemplars protect
themselves. ORG_DENY_SEED covers grantee names that appear outside that structure.

Run: uniclaude-brain-daily [--dry] [--preflight [--against <script>]]
  --dry        distil and report, capture nothing
  --preflight  render every source and say whether a change is safe to ship;
               with --against <script>, diff against that copy of this script.
               Reads only: no lane refresh, no capture, no heartbeat.
"""
